<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Dec producer price index up 8.8 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African Dec producer price index up 8.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities producer price index rose 1.0 percent in December from November after rising 0.5 percent in November, Central Statistical Service figures show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in December was 8.8 percent after November's 8.5 percent rise.</p>
<p>The service said that for 1996 as a whole, producer inflation averaged 6.9 percent compared with 9.6 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast December PPI would rise 0.9 percent month-on-month and 8.7 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 Dec '96   Nov '96   Dec '95  - latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities    8.8	 8.5	 8.5	  1.0	0.5</p>
<p>Locally produced   8.5	 8.8	 9.2	  0.7	0.5</p>
<p>Imported	     9.3	 7.8	 5.8	  1.8	0.1</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 Dec '96   Nov '96   Dec '95</p>
<p>All commodities    111.4     110.3     102.4</p>
<p>Locally produced   111.9     111.1     103.1</p>
<p>Imported	     110.0     108.1     100.6</p>
